Sat Oct 31 10:40:12 AM UTC 2026
$PROBLEM Warfarin IOV (CL) - IMP estimation with inter-occasion variability (#2301)
; Same model, data and initial estimates as warfarin_iov_impmap.ctl; only the
; method differs (IMP: MAP on the first iteration only, then the proposal is
; re-centred on the previous iteration's sample moments — ferx `method = imp`).
; IOV is written NONMEM's way: one ETA per occasion sharing a variance via
; BLOCK(1) SAME, which ferx spells `kappa`.
$DATA warfarin_iov.csv IGNORE=@
$INPUT ID TIME DV EVID AMT CMT=DROP RATE MDV OCC
$SUBROUTINES ADVAN2 TRANS2
$PK
  OCC1 = 0
  OCC2 = 0
  IF(OCC.EQ.1) OCC1 = 1
  IF(OCC.EQ.2) OCC2 = 1
  IOVCL = OCC1*ETA(4) + OCC2*ETA(5)
  CL = THETA(1)*EXP(ETA(1) + IOVCL)
  V  = THETA(2)*EXP(ETA(2))
  KA = THETA(3)*EXP(ETA(3))
  S2 = V
$ERROR
  IPRED = F
  Y = IPRED*(1 + EPS(1))
$THETA (0, 0.2)   ; TVCL
$THETA (0, 10.0)  ; TVV
$THETA (0, 1.5)   ; TVKA
$OMEGA 0.09       ; ETA_CL  (BSV)
$OMEGA 0.04       ; ETA_V   (BSV)
$OMEGA 0.30       ; ETA_KA  (BSV)
$OMEGA BLOCK(1) 0.01   ; KAPPA_CL occasion 1
$OMEGA BLOCK(1) SAME   ; KAPPA_CL occasion 2 (same variance => IOV)
$SIGMA 0.04       ; proportional variance (= 0.2 SD, the .ferx init)
$ESTIMATION METHOD=IMP INTERACTION NITER=200 ISAMPLE=300 PRINT=1 SEED=12345 NOABORT

NM-TRAN MESSAGES
  
 WARNINGS AND ERRORS (IF ANY) FOR PROBLEM    1
             
 (WARNING  2) NM-TRAN INFERS THAT THE DATA ARE POPULATION.
  
Note: Analytical 2nd Derivatives are constructed in FSUBS but are never used.
      You may insert $ABBR DERIV2=NO after the first $PROB to save FSUBS construction and compilation time
  

